{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760837314,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e015072e001cdI8WvgIZOgmTq","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e0145ee3001RV3SGaGab1eHM2","type":"tool","id":"call_3376bb51db814c6aa102efa2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 1-215\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\"\n3: description: \"Vitest, Python and fixture coverage for skill-advisor routing, handlers, hooks, schemas, scorer paths and compatibility behavior.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor tests\"\n6:   - \"advisor regression tests\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor vitest\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/tests/` is the regression surface for the skill-advisor package. It groups focused Vitest suites, compatibility checks, handler and hook tests, schema checks, Python parity tests and shared fixtures used by the advisor scorer and daemon paths.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Covers advisor routing, scorer, lane attribution, cache, daemon freshness and lifecycle metadata behavior.\n21: - Keeps compatibility, parity and schema tests in named subfolders.\n22: - Provides shared fixtures and helpers used across direct TypeScript and Python-facing advisor checks.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR TESTS                         │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Test runner  │ ───▶ │ Vitest suites   │ ───▶ │ Advisor modules  │\n35: │ npm / vitest │      │ tests/*.ts      │      │ lib / handlers   │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Fixtures      │ ───▶   │ Schemas        │\n41:                       │ tests/fixtures│        │ schemas/*      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Python parity │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: test suites -> fixtures -> advisor runtime modules\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: tests/\n58: +-- cache/                   # Cache behavior coverage\n59: +-- compat/                  # Compatibility contract checks\n60: +-- fixtures/                # Prompt, graph and routing fixtures\n61: +-- helpers/                 # Test-only helpers (env snapshot, activation-matrix evidence)\n62: +-- handlers/                # Handler tests\n63: +-- hooks/                   # Hook integration tests\n64: +-- legacy/                  # Legacy compatibility coverage\n65: +-- parity/                  # Cross-runtime parity checks\n66: +-- python/                  # Python wrapper and script tests\n67: +-- schemas/                 # Schema validation tests\n68: +-- scorer/                  # Native scorer tests\n69: +-- embedders/               # Embedder schema and shared parity tests\n70: +-- skill-graph/             # Skill-graph round-trip tests\n71: +-- *.vitest.ts              # Package-level regression suites\n72: +-- *.test.ts                # Focused unit tests\n73: `-- README.md\n74: ```\n75: \n76: Allowed direction:\n77: \n78: ```text\n79: tests -> fixtures\n80: tests -> skill_advisor/lib\n81: tests -> skill_advisor/handlers\n82: ```\n83: \n84: Disallowed direction:\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: runtime code -> tests\n88: fixtures -> generated runtime state without an explicit test setup\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: tests/\n97: +-- affordance-normalizer.test.ts\n98: +-- advisor-rebuild.vitest.ts\n99: +-- command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts\n100: +-- command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts\n101: +-- command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n102: +-- cross-skill-edges.vitest.ts\n103: +-- daemon-freshness-foundation.vitest.ts\n104: +-- daemon-watcher-resource-leaks-049-005.vitest.ts\n105: +-- lane-attribution.test.ts\n106: +-- launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts\n107: +-- launcher-idle-timeout.vitest.ts\n108: +-- launcher-lease.vitest.ts\n109: +-- launcher-reap-pid-reuse.vitest.ts\n110: +-- lifecycle-derived-metadata.vitest.ts\n111: +-- manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\n112: +-- migration-lineage-identity.vitest.ts\n113: +-- prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts\n114: +-- system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts\n115: +-- rename-invariants.vitest.ts\n116: +-- routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts\n117: +-- routing-parity-deep-skills.vitest.ts\n118: +-- routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\n119: +-- shadow-sink.vitest.ts\n120: +-- skill-advisor-cli-dual-client.vitest.ts\n121: +-- skill-advisor-cli-help-aliases-errors.vitest.ts\n122: +-- skill-advisor-cli-job-semantics.vitest.ts\n123: +-- skill-advisor-cli-manifest-parity.vitest.ts\n124: +-- skill-advisor-cli-parity.vitest.ts\n125: +-- skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts\n126: +-- skill-advisor-cli-trusted-prompt-time.vitest.ts\n127: +-- skill-advisor-launcher-orphan-reaping.vitest.ts\n128: +-- skill-doc-harvest.vitest.ts\n129: +-- skill-graph-bfs-traversal.vitest.ts\n130: +-- skill-graph-db.vitest.ts\n131: +-- skill-graph-diagnostic-redaction.vitest.ts\n132: +-- skill-graph-handlers.vitest.ts\n133: +-- skill-graph-queries-parity.vitest.ts\n134: +-- sqlite-integrity.vitest.ts\n135: +-- tsconfig.tests.json\n136: +-- embedders/\n137: +-- skill-graph/\n138: +-- scorer/\n139: `-- README.md\n140: ```\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: ## 5. KEY FILES\n145: \n146: | File | Responsibility |\n147: |---|---|\n148: | `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n149: | `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n150: | `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n151: | `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n152: | `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n153: | `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |\n154: | `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n155: | `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n156: | `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n157: | `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n158: | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n159: | `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n160: | `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n161: | `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n166: \n167: | Boundary | Rule |\n168: |---|---|\n169: | Imports | Tests may import advisor runtime modules, schemas, fixtures and local shared helpers. |\n170: | Exports | This folder exports no production runtime code. |\n171: | Ownership | Keep advisor package tests here. Put code-graph, memory or deep-loop tests in their own package folders. |\n172: \n173: Main flow:\n174: \n175: ```text\n176: fixture or inline scenario\n177:   -> advisor scorer, handler, hook or schema path\n178:   -> prompt-safe result, metadata or validation output\n179:   -> assertion on stable advisor behavior\n180: ```\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n185: \n186: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n187: |---|---|---|\n188: | `*.vitest.ts` | Test files | Vitest regression suites for daemon, lifecycle, shadow and database behavior. |\n189: | `*.test.ts` | Test files | Focused unit tests for affordance and attribution helpers. |\n190: | `fixtures/` | Test data | Shared prompt and routing inputs. |\n191: | `scorer/` | Test folder | Native scorer regression coverage. |\n192: | `embedders/` | Test folder | Embedder boundary and schema coverage. |\n193: | `skill-graph/` | Test folder | Focused skill-graph database coverage. |\n194: \n195: ---\n196: \n197: ## 8. VALIDATION\n198: \n199: Run from the repository root.\n200: \n201: ```bash\n202: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n203: ```\n204: \n205: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n206: \n207: ---\n208: \n209: ## 9. RELATED\n210: \n211: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n212: - [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n213: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n214: - [`skill-graph/README.md`](skill-graph/README.md)\n215: - [`scorer/README.md`](scorer/README.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md, lines 1-215\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\"\n3: description: \"Vitest, Python and fixture coverage for skill-advisor routing, handlers, hooks, schemas, scorer paths and compatibility behavior.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor tests\"\n6:   - \"advisor regression tests\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor vitest\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Tests: Regression And Contract Coverage\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/tests/` is the regression surface for the skill-advisor package. It groups focused Vitest suites, compatibility checks, handler and hook tests, schema checks, Python parity tests and shared fixtures used by the advisor scorer and daemon paths.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Covers advisor routing, scorer, lane attribution, cache, daemon freshness and lifecycle metadata behavior.\n21: - Keeps compatibility, parity and schema tests in named subfolders.\n22: - Provides shared fixtures and helpers used across direct TypeScript and Python-facing advisor checks.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR TESTS                         │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Test runner  │ ───▶ │ Vitest suites   │ ───▶ │ Advisor modules  │\n35: │ npm / vitest │      │ tests/*.ts      │      │ lib / handlers   │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Fixtures      │ ───▶   │ Schemas        │\n41:                       │ tests/fixtures│        │ schemas/*      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Python parity │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: test suites -> fixtures -> advisor runtime modules\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: tests/\n58: +-- cache/                   # Cache behavior coverage\n59: +-- compat/                  # Compatibility contract checks\n60: +-- fixtures/                # Prompt, graph and routing fixtures\n61: +-- helpers/                 # Test-only helpers (env snapshot, activation-matrix evidence)\n62: +-- handlers/                # Handler tests\n63: +-- hooks/                   # Hook integration tests\n64: +-- legacy/                  # Legacy compatibility coverage\n65: +-- parity/                  # Cross-runtime parity checks\n66: +-- python/                  # Python wrapper and script tests\n67: +-- schemas/                 # Schema validation tests\n68: +-- scorer/                  # Native scorer tests\n69: +-- embedders/               # Embedder schema and shared parity tests\n70: +-- skill-graph/             # Skill-graph round-trip tests\n71: +-- *.vitest.ts              # Package-level regression suites\n72: +-- *.test.ts                # Focused unit tests\n73: `-- README.md\n74: ```\n75: \n76: Allowed direction:\n77: \n78: ```text\n79: tests -> fixtures\n80: tests -> skill_advisor/lib\n81: tests -> skill_advisor/handlers\n82: ```\n83: \n84: Disallowed direction:\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: runtime code -> tests\n88: fixtures -> generated runtime state without an explicit test setup\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: tests/\n97: +-- affordance-normalizer.test.ts\n98: +-- advisor-rebuild.vitest.ts\n99: +-- command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts\n100: +-- command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts\n101: +-- command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n102: +-- cross-skill-edges.vitest.ts\n103: +-- daemon-freshness-foundation.vitest.ts\n104: +-- daemon-watcher-resource-leaks-049-005.vitest.ts\n105: +-- lane-attribution.test.ts\n106: +-- launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts\n107: +-- launcher-idle-timeout.vitest.ts\n108: +-- launcher-lease.vitest.ts\n109: +-- launcher-reap-pid-reuse.vitest.ts\n110: +-- lifecycle-derived-metadata.vitest.ts\n111: +-- manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts\n112: +-- migration-lineage-identity.vitest.ts\n113: +-- prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts\n114: +-- system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts\n115: +-- rename-invariants.vitest.ts\n116: +-- routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts\n117: +-- routing-parity-deep-skills.vitest.ts\n118: +-- routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\n119: +-- shadow-sink.vitest.ts\n120: +-- skill-advisor-cli-dual-client.vitest.ts\n121: +-- skill-advisor-cli-help-aliases-errors.vitest.ts\n122: +-- skill-advisor-cli-job-semantics.vitest.ts\n123: +-- skill-advisor-cli-manifest-parity.vitest.ts\n124: +-- skill-advisor-cli-parity.vitest.ts\n125: +-- skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts\n126: +-- skill-advisor-cli-trusted-prompt-time.vitest.ts\n127: +-- skill-advisor-launcher-orphan-reaping.vitest.ts\n128: +-- skill-doc-harvest.vitest.ts\n129: +-- skill-graph-bfs-traversal.vitest.ts\n130: +-- skill-graph-db.vitest.ts\n131: +-- skill-graph-diagnostic-redaction.vitest.ts\n132: +-- skill-graph-handlers.vitest.ts\n133: +-- skill-graph-queries-parity.vitest.ts\n134: +-- sqlite-integrity.vitest.ts\n135: +-- tsconfig.tests.json\n136: +-- embedders/\n137: +-- skill-graph/\n138: +-- scorer/\n139: `-- README.md\n140: ```\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: ## 5. KEY FILES\n145: \n146: | File | Responsibility |\n147: |---|---|\n148: | `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n149: | `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n150: | `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n151: | `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n152: | `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n153: | `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |\n154: | `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n155: | `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n156: | `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 28 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, a meaning pass must also clear the uncertainty bar, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n157: | `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n158: | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n159: | `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n160: | `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n161: | `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n166: \n167: | Boundary | Rule |\n168: |---|---|\n169: | Imports | Tests may import advisor runtime modules, schemas, fixtures and local shared helpers. |\n170: | Exports | This folder exports no production runtime code. |\n171: | Ownership | Keep advisor package tests here. Put code-graph, memory or deep-loop tests in their own package folders. |\n172: \n173: Main flow:\n174: \n175: ```text\n176: fixture or inline scenario\n177:   -> advisor scorer, handler, hook or schema path\n178:   -> prompt-safe result, metadata or validation output\n179:   -> assertion on stable advisor behavior\n180: ```\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n185: \n186: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n187: |---|---|---|\n188: | `*.vitest.ts` | Test files | Vitest regression suites for daemon, lifecycle, shadow and database behavior. |\n189: | `*.test.ts` | Test files | Focused unit tests for affordance and attribution helpers. |\n190: | `fixtures/` | Test data | Shared prompt and routing inputs. |\n191: | `scorer/` | Test folder | Native scorer regression coverage. |\n192: | `embedders/` | Test folder | Embedder boundary and schema coverage. |\n193: | `skill-graph/` | Test folder | Focused skill-graph database coverage. |\n194: \n195: ---\n196: \n197: ## 8. VALIDATION\n198: \n199: Run from the repository root.\n200: \n201: ```bash\n202: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\n203: ```\n204: \n205: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n206: \n207: ---\n208: \n209: ## 9. RELATED\n210: \n211: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n212: - [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n213: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n214: - [`skill-graph/README.md`](skill-graph/README.md)\n215: - [`scorer/README.md`](scorer/README.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760836910,"end":1794760837314}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760837359,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e015002f001QSqxfFLzCd3cTN","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e0145ee3001RV3SGaGab1eHM2","type":"tool","id":"call_575cc63fe030471aa454ded7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\necho \"== history + noedit in command-attach\"; grep -n \"HISTORY\\|history\\|NO_EDIT_REQUEST\\|isNoEditRequest\\|DECLINE\\|ASK_LEADS\\|CORRECTION\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | head -30\necho \"== vibe child\"; sed -n '200,240p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs\necho \"== DOC ids 385-391\"; grep -l \"^id: DOC-3\" .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/*.md >/dev/null 2>&1; grep -h \"^id: DOC-3\" .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/*.md | sort | head -20"},"output":"== history + noedit in command-attach\n334:const CORRECTION_VERB = /\\b(?:fix|correct|update|edit|change|tweak|repair)\\b/;\n348:export const NO_EDIT_REQUEST = /\\b(no edits?|make no changes|no changes yet|without making changes|(?:do not|don't|dont) (?:make (?:any )?changes|change|edit|modify|touch|(?:create|write|add|delete|remove) (?:it|this|that|anything|any files?))|read-only only|no edits yet|only; do not|just show|just list)\\b/;\n352:export function isNoEditRequest(text: string): boolean {\n353:  return NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(text.toLowerCase().replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\"));\n371:export const COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS: readonly string[] = [\n389:export const COMMAND_ASK_LEADS: readonly string[] = [\n428:    const led = COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n430:    )) || COMMAND_ASK_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n483:  if (isNoEditRequest(prompt)) return undefined;\n502:    && CORRECTION_VERB.test(prompt.toLowerCase())\n== vibe child\n * @param {Object} [dependencies] - Injectable for deterministic tests.\n * @returns {Promise<string>} The advisor brief, or an empty string.\n */\nexport async function buildAdvisorPart(payload, {\n  run = runAdvisor,\n  env = process.env,\n  isEnabled = isHookEnabled,\n  read = readHeadReceipt,\n  write = writeHeadReceipt,\n} = {}) {\n  try {\n    if (!payload || payload.hook_event_name !== 'pre_agent') return '';\n    if (isChildSession(payload, env)) return '';\n\n    const prompt = typeof payload.prompt === 'string' ? payload.prompt : '';\n    if (!prompt.trim()) return '';\n    if (isEnabled('skill-advisor') === false) return '';\n\n    const sessionId = typeof payload.session_id === 'string' ? payload.session_id : '';\n    const transcriptPath = typeof payload.transcript_path === 'string' && payload.transcript_path\n      ? payload.transcript_path\n      : undefined;\n    const output = await run({\n      prompt,\n      cwd: REPO_ROOT,\n      session_id: sessionId,\n      transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n      hook_event_name: 'UserPromptSubmit',\n    });\n\n    const context = output?.hookSpecificOutput?.additionalContext;\n    if (typeof context !== 'string' || !context.trim()) return '';\n    return reduceRepeatedHead(withCommandDocuments(context), sessionId, { read, write });\n  } catch {\n    return '';\n  }\n}\n== DOC ids 385-391\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"== history + noedit in command-attach\n334:const CORRECTION_VERB = /\\b(?:fix|correct|update|edit|change|tweak|repair)\\b/;\n348:export const NO_EDIT_REQUEST = /\\b(no edits?|make no changes|no changes yet|without making changes|(?:do not|don't|dont) (?:make (?:any )?changes|change|edit|modify|touch|(?:create|write|add|delete|remove) (?:it|this|that|anything|any files?))|read-only only|no edits yet|only; do not|just show|just list)\\b/;\n352:export function isNoEditRequest(text: string): boolean {\n353:  return NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(text.toLowerCase().replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\"));\n371:export const COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS: readonly string[] = [\n389:export const COMMAND_ASK_LEADS: readonly string[] = [\n428:    const led = COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n430:    )) || COMMAND_ASK_LEADS.some((lead) => (\n483:  if (isNoEditRequest(prompt)) return undefined;\n502:    && CORRECTION_VERB.test(prompt.toLowerCase())\n== vibe child\n * @param {Object} [dependencies] - Injectable for deterministic tests.\n * @returns {Promise<string>} The advisor brief, or an empty string.\n */\nexport async function buildAdvisorPart(payload, {\n  run = runAdvisor,\n  env = process.env,\n  isEnabled = isHookEnabled,\n  read = readHeadReceipt,\n  write = writeHeadReceipt,\n} = {}) {\n  try {\n    if (!payload || payload.hook_event_name !== 'pre_agent') return '';\n    if (isChildSession(payload, env)) return '';\n\n    const prompt = typeof payload.prompt === 'string' ? payload.prompt : '';\n    if (!prompt.trim()) return '';\n    if (isEnabled('skill-advisor') === false) return '';\n\n    const sessionId = typeof payload.session_id === 'string' ? payload.session_id : '';\n    const transcriptPath = typeof payload.transcript_path === 'string' && payload.transcript_path\n      ? payload.transcript_path\n      : undefined;\n    const output = await run({\n      prompt,\n      cwd: REPO_ROOT,\n      session_id: sessionId,\n      transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n      hook_event_name: 'UserPromptSubmit',\n    });\n\n    const context = output?.hookSpecificOutput?.additionalContext;\n    if (typeof context !== 'string' || !context.trim()) return '';\n    return reduceRepeatedHead(withCommandDocuments(context), sessionId, { read, write });\n  } catch {\n    return '';\n  }\n}\n== DOC ids 385-391\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\necho \\\"== history + noedit in command-attach\\\"; grep -n \\\"HISTORY\\\\|history\\\\|NO_EDIT_REQUEST\\\\|isNoEditRequest\\\\|DECLINE\\\\|ASK_LEADS\\\\|CORRECTION\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | head -30\\necho \\\"== vibe child\\\"; sed -n '200,240p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs\\necho \\\"== DOC ids 385-391\\\"; grep -l \\\"^id: DOC-3\\\" .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/*.md >/dev/null 2>&1; grep -h \\\"^id: DOC-3\\\" .skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/*.md | sort | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760835119,"end":1794760837359}}}}
