{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760897631,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e015ed79002CvqgzftpmrtTcX","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e015cf94001Vg9k5vb8SWCcXE","type":"tool","id":"call_25fd141d629e47b4a51c9a85","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\necho \"== hook-flags value rule\"; grep -n \"=== '1'\\|=== \\\"1\\\"\\|truthy\\|TRUTHY\\|parseFlag\\|isEnabled\\|enabled =\" .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs | head -30\necho \"== vibe runAdvisor import\"; grep -n \"runAdvisor\\|import\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs | head -20\necho \"== health write in fallback\"; grep -n \"health\\|record\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts | head -20\necho \"== hook doc runtimes\"; grep -n \"Codex\\|Cursor\\|Devin\\|DSH\\|Vibe\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20"},"output":"== hook-flags value rule\n157:  return v === \"1\" || v === \"true\" || v === \"yes\" || v === \"on\";\n298:// True when one named switch resolves truthy, for a switch that is not a hook\n== vibe runAdvisor import\n16:import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n17:import { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n18:import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n19:import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n20:import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n22:import { isHookEnabled } from '../../../../hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs';\n30:const REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n34:  import.meta.url,\n184:async function runAdvisor(input) {\n185:  const advisor = await import(ADVISOR_MODULE_URL);\n204:  run = runAdvisor,\n== health write in fallback\n514:      // The health record counts degraded answers, and only this step knows the\n== hook doc runtimes\n3:description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n23:The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). DSH carries a `repo-guards` adapter that imports the same compiled handler in-process. OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n84:Every native runtime, Pi and DSH run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n89:| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90:| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91:| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n94:| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` (real file, reached through the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` symlink) | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n95:| **Vibe** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`, called by `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs` | `pre_agent` in `.vibe/hooks.toml` (`turn-start`, match `main`), rendered into a dispatch's `VIBE_HOME` | Proxies the operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `vibe`. A child dispatch and a subagent turn get no brief | `hook_specific_output.additional_context`; the routing head and directives repeat only when they change, because Vibe keeps added context in the conversation. A head that names a command gains one line naming each command's document under `.skilled/commands/`, because Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form |\n106:| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107:| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108:| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n111:| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n127:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n132:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real Vibe part (the turn-start composer calls it)\n196:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n253:This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"== hook-flags value rule\n157:  return v === \"1\" || v === \"true\" || v === \"yes\" || v === \"on\";\n298:// True when one named switch resolves truthy, for a switch that is not a hook\n== vibe runAdvisor import\n16:import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n17:import { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n18:import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n19:import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n20:import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n22:import { isHookEnabled } from '../../../../hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs';\n30:const REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n34:  import.meta.url,\n184:async function runAdvisor(input) {\n185:  const advisor = await import(ADVISOR_MODULE_URL);\n204:  run = runAdvisor,\n== health write in fallback\n514:      // The health record counts degraded answers, and only this step knows the\n== hook doc runtimes\n3:description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n23:The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). DSH carries a `repo-guards` adapter that imports the same compiled handler in-process. OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n84:Every native runtime, Pi and DSH run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n89:| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90:| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91:| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n94:| **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` (real file, reached through the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` symlink) | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n95:| **Vibe** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`, called by `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs` | `pre_agent` in `.vibe/hooks.toml` (`turn-start`, match `main`), rendered into a dispatch's `VIBE_HOME` | Proxies the operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `vibe`. A child dispatch and a subagent turn get no brief | `hook_specific_output.additional_context`; the routing head and directives repeat only when they change, because Vibe keeps added context in the conversation. A head that names a command gains one line naming each command's document under `.skilled/commands/`, because Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form |\n106:| Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107:| Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108:| Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n111:| DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n127:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n132:|   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real Vibe part (the turn-start composer calls it)\n196:| Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n253:This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\necho \\\"== hook-flags value rule\\\"; grep -n \\\"=== '1'\\\\|=== \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"\\\\|truthy\\\\|TRUTHY\\\\|parseFlag\\\\|isEnabled\\\\|enabled =\\\" .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs | head -30\\necho \\\"== vibe runAdvisor import\\\"; grep -n \\\"runAdvisor\\\\|import\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs | head -20\\necho \\\"== health write in fallback\\\"; grep -n \\\"health\\\\|record\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts | head -20\\necho \\\"== hook doc runtimes\\\"; grep -n \\\"Codex\\\\|Cursor\\\\|Devin\\\\|DSH\\\\|Vibe\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760895865,"end":1794760897631}}}}
