{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761452954,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"id":"prt_1e01e6d9a0016XLNWRcHA0D93h","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e01e5a01001zeQKnBWT8426KZ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"90dab8dbe7197079e87b586dab2f8f14095f7123"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761497778,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01ecc4500166yo1jlxI9Lx6i","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e01e5a01001zeQKnBWT8426KZ","type":"tool","id":"call_9dac7af996174a60bbc2ba5a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dimension\n\nPrimary dimension: **maintainability**. The pass tested whether the two hand-maintained inventories in the scoped package still describe the files and verdicts they claim, and whether the structural defects raised in iteration 1 have a single root cause or several.\n\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus asks for docs against code across the `docs-metadata` area. This iteration concentrated on the two packages whose structure iteration 1 flagged — the manual-testing playbook and the tests README — and re-checked their inventories against the live tree. It also carried the operator focus's holdout-hygiene and command-offer questions forward without opening any prompt corpus.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `docs-metadata-5`.\n- Session: `fanout-docs-metadata-5-1794760565927-i99t40`, generation 1, new lineage.\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes. Consumed: 6 calls, about 2 minutes.\n- Prior state: 6 open P2 findings, 0 P0, 0 P1, traceability covered.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:27-363`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:54-215`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts:44-77`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/command-offer-fit-gates.md:16-133`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:16-198`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:16-151`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The playbook's scenario verdict set disagrees with its result-persistence contract** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:30` -- The result-persistence contract says a scenario run is complete only after its \"`PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome\". The review protocol defines four scenario verdicts and adds `PARTIAL`, then requires triage notes for it: \"`PASS`: all acceptance checks true. `PARTIAL`: core behavior works but non-critical evidence or metadata is incomplete.\" at line 121, and \"Triage notes for every `FAIL`, `PARTIAL` or `SKIP`\" at line 84. The release rule at line 133 then counts only `PASS` or an approved `SKIP`. No document in the package defines where a `PARTIAL` record lives.\n   - Case: an operator runs a scenario whose core behavior works but whose evidence capture is incomplete; the protocol tells them to record `PARTIAL`, and the persistence contract gives that outcome no defined slot, so the run cannot be recorded as complete.\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:30]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:119]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:84]`.\n   - User impact: the same package defines a verdict and then cannot persist it, which makes the manual-validation record ambiguous at exactly the partial-evidence case the protocol anticipates.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \"PARTIAL\"` over the package returns the scenario-verdict definition, the feature-verdict rules and the triage requirement; the persistence contract and release rule name only three outcomes, so this is a vocabulary split inside one document rather than a second convention.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"manual testing playbook: result persistence\", \"manual testing playbook: scenario verdicts\", \"release readiness rule\"]\n   - Recommendation: add `PARTIAL` to the persistence contract with its storage rule, or drop it from the scenario verdicts and treat partial evidence as `FAIL`.\n\n## Refined Findings\n\n- DM5-P2-003 (Wave 2 schedules an unauthored scenario): the root cause is that the wave plan and the category table are two hand-maintained inventories of the same 53 files. The plan already drifted from the table. A single generated inventory would have prevented the CL-004 entry.\n- DM5-P2-005 (tests README tree): the tree is hand-maintained against 91 files and has drifted by 52. Generating it, or replacing it with a stable subfolder map, removes the recurring cost.\n\nBoth refinements are recorded as context for remediation; they are not re-counted as new findings.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | No top-level `spec.md` reference to these docs; phase child `025-release-notes-and-doc-sync` owns the release-note intent. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`; phase children own their checklists. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The scoped docs remain consistent with the skill's routing and playbook pointers. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Vibe and Claude surfaces checked in iteration 1; Codex, Cursor and Devin remain outside scope. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | No catalog claim changed; iteration 1's two advisories remain open. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | Inventory and verdict vocabulary checked; one new advisory. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` asserts the 53-row inventory, the 53-file category tree and the persistence-contract strings by exact substring, which is why the `PARTIAL` split survives every test run: the test pins line 30's three outcomes and never reads the verdict section.\n- `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3 names 13 subfolders and section 4 draws only 3 of them; the 13 named subfolders all exist, so the topology prose is accurate and the tree is the stale half.\n- The central doctor playbook link at `manual-testing-playbook.md:303` resolves to `.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `PARTIAL` could be read as a feature-level verdict only. It is reported because section 5 places it under \"Scenario verdict\" before the separate \"Feature Verdict Rules\" section, and section 3 requires triage notes for a `PARTIAL` scenario.\n- The wave plan could be read as advisory rather than executable. It is reported because section 6 calls it the \"Recommended Wave Plan\" for operators and assigns scenario IDs before parallel execution.\n- The tests README tree could be intentionally partial. It is reported because its heading is \"DIRECTORY TREE\" and it lists files rather than a curated subset; a reader cannot tell omission from absence.\n- No prompt corpus was opened in this iteration. Holdout hygiene holds; the only holdout references in the package remain aggregate metric names in sibling documents.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- All 13 subfolders named in `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3 exist.\n- All five files named in the same README's sections 4 and 5 exist: `affordance-normalizer.test.ts`, `lane-attribution.test.ts`, `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts`, `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` and `tsconfig.tests.json`.\n- The central doctor playbook referenced by `manual-testing-playbook.md:303` exists.\n- Every section-table scenario link in the root playbook resolves; the playbook inventory test's exact substrings are present in the root document.\n- No scope violation occurred; no file outside the lineage directory was written.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A tests-README subfolder that does not exist: none; 13 of 13 named subfolders are present.\n- A tests-README key file that does not exist: none; 5 of 5 named files are present.\n- A broken central-playbook link: none.\n- A second, hidden scenario-verdict vocabulary: none found; the split is between the persistence contract and the verdict section only.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the workflow-measure section of the changelog against `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` — the load-rate numerator, the followed-rate numerator, the published path count, and the Vibe journal normalization.\n- Reason: the operator focus names the transcript scorer's load, followed-step and offer counting, and that section is the one scoped document whose formulas have not yet been checked against code.\n- Rotation status: traceability and maintainability completed; correctness and security remain.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — the maintainability pass found one new vocabulary split and closed two structural questions.\n- Required evidence: the `loadRate` and `followedRate` expressions, the `workflowPath()` return union, and the Vibe journal loader path.\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nPrimary dimension: **maintainability**. The pass tested whether the two hand-maintained inventories in the scoped package still describe the files and verdicts they claim, and whether the structural defects raised in iteration 1 have a single root cause or several.\\n\\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus asks for docs against code across the `docs-metadata` area. This iteration concentrated on the two packages whose structure iteration 1 flagged — the manual-testing playbook and the tests README — and re-checked their inventories against the live tree. It also carried the operator focus's holdout-hygiene and command-offer questions forward without opening any prompt corpus.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `docs-metadata-5`.\\n- Session: `fanout-docs-metadata-5-1794760565927-i99t40`, generation 1, new lineage.\\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes. Consumed: 6 calls, about 2 minutes.\\n- Prior state: 6 open P2 findings, 0 P0, 0 P1, traceability covered.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:27-363`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:54-215`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts:44-77`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/command-offer-fit-gates.md:16-133`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:16-198`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:16-151`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The playbook's scenario verdict set disagrees with its result-persistence contract** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:30` -- The result-persistence contract says a scenario run is complete only after its \\\"`PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome\\\". The review protocol defines four scenario verdicts and adds `PARTIAL`, then requires triage notes for it: \\\"`PASS`: all acceptance checks true. `PARTIAL`: core behavior works but non-critical evidence or metadata is incomplete.\\\" at line 121, and \\\"Triage notes for every `FAIL`, `PARTIAL` or `SKIP`\\\" at line 84. The release rule at line 133 then counts only `PASS` or an approved `SKIP`. No document in the package defines where a `PARTIAL` record lives.\\n   - Case: an operator runs a scenario whose core behavior works but whose evidence capture is incomplete; the protocol tells them to record `PARTIAL`, and the persistence contract gives that outcome no defined slot, so the run cannot be recorded as complete.\\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:30]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:119]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:84]`.\\n   - User impact: the same package defines a verdict and then cannot persist it, which makes the manual-validation record ambiguous at exactly the partial-evidence case the protocol anticipates.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: `rg -n \\\"PARTIAL\\\"` over the package returns the scenario-verdict definition, the feature-verdict rules and the triage requirement; the persistence contract and release rule name only three outcomes, so this is a vocabulary split inside one document rather than a second convention.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"manual testing playbook: result persistence\\\", \\\"manual testing playbook: scenario verdicts\\\", \\\"release readiness rule\\\"]\\n   - Recommendation: add `PARTIAL` to the persistence contract with its storage rule, or drop it from the scenario verdicts and treat partial evidence as `FAIL`.\\n\\n## Refined Findings\\n\\n- DM5-P2-003 (Wave 2 schedules an unauthored scenario): the root cause is that the wave plan and the category table are two hand-maintained inventories of the same 53 files. The plan already drifted from the table. A single generated inventory would have prevented the CL-004 entry.\\n- DM5-P2-005 (tests README tree): the tree is hand-maintained against 91 files and has drifted by 52. Generating it, or replacing it with a stable subfolder map, removes the recurring cost.\\n\\nBoth refinements are recorded as context for remediation; they are not re-counted as new findings.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | No top-level `spec.md` reference to these docs; phase child `025-release-notes-and-doc-sync` owns the release-note intent. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`; phase children own their checklists. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The scoped docs remain consistent with the skill's routing and playbook pointers. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Vibe and Claude surfaces checked in iteration 1; Codex, Cursor and Devin remain outside scope. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | No catalog claim changed; iteration 1's two advisories remain open. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | Inventory and verdict vocabulary checked; one new advisory. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` asserts the 53-row inventory, the 53-file category tree and the persistence-contract strings by exact substring, which is why the `PARTIAL` split survives every test run: the test pins line 30's three outcomes and never reads the verdict section.\\n- `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3 names 13 subfolders and section 4 draws only 3 of them; the 13 named subfolders all exist, so the topology prose is accurate and the tree is the stale half.\\n- The central doctor playbook link at `manual-testing-playbook.md:303` resolves to `.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `PARTIAL` could be read as a feature-level verdict only. It is reported because section 5 places it under \\\"Scenario verdict\\\" before the separate \\\"Feature Verdict Rules\\\" section, and section 3 requires triage notes for a `PARTIAL` scenario.\\n- The wave plan could be read as advisory rather than executable. It is reported because section 6 calls it the \\\"Recommended Wave Plan\\\" for operators and assigns scenario IDs before parallel execution.\\n- The tests README tree could be intentionally partial. It is reported because its heading is \\\"DIRECTORY TREE\\\" and it lists files rather than a curated subset; a reader cannot tell omission from absence.\\n- No prompt corpus was opened in this iteration. Holdout hygiene holds; the only holdout references in the package remain aggregate metric names in sibling documents.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- All 13 subfolders named in `runtime/tests/README.md` section 3 exist.\\n- All five files named in the same README's sections 4 and 5 exist: `affordance-normalizer.test.ts`, `lane-attribution.test.ts`, `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts`, `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` and `tsconfig.tests.json`.\\n- The central doctor playbook referenced by `manual-testing-playbook.md:303` exists.\\n- Every section-table scenario link in the root playbook resolves; the playbook inventory test's exact substrings are present in the root document.\\n- No scope violation occurred; no file outside the lineage directory was written.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A tests-README subfolder that does not exist: none; 13 of 13 named subfolders are present.\\n- A tests-README key file that does not exist: none; 5 of 5 named files are present.\\n- A broken central-playbook link: none.\\n- A second, hidden scenario-verdict vocabulary: none found; the split is between the persistence contract and the verdict section only.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the workflow-measure section of the changelog against `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` — the load-rate numerator, the followed-rate numerator, the published path count, and the Vibe journal normalization.\\n- Reason: the operator focus names the transcript scorer's load, followed-step and offer counting, and that section is the one scoped document whose formulas have not yet been checked against code.\\n- Rotation status: traceability and maintainability completed; correctness and security remain.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — the maintainability pass found one new vocabulary split and closed two structural questions.\\n- Required evidence: the `loadRate` and `followedRate` expressions, the `workflowPath()` return union, and the Vibe journal loader path.\\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761477189,"end":1794761497778}}}}
