{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761605148,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e020bac1002I5n0w2j2zS95YA","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e02084ea0018MavfHKUVDdJFf","type":"tool","id":"call_f00969fa178b40cb831da443","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\nsed -n '172,200p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\necho \"== vibe advisor module\"; sed -n '24,40p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs; sed -n '180,200p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs\necho \"== health writer name\"; grep -n \"export.*record\\|appendAdvisorHookDiagnostic\\|writeAdvisorHook\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts | head"},"output":"## Workflow Measure\n\n#### Six Paths and Two Rates\n\nThe transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n\n#### Every Shape a Load Takes\n\nA load is a read tool, a skill tool or a shell read. The shell readers include `cat`, `sed -n` and `head`. An in-place `sed` is not a read. A `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror counts too. On Codex, one `exec_command` body counts as one shell step.\n\n#### What Does Not Count\n\nA search is not a load, and neither is a heredoc line. A write outside the checkout, such as a temp note, no longer sets the boundary for a load.\n\n#### The Counts on Sealed Rows\n\nNobody tuned the 44 sealed plain rows. The brief carries the right command 1 time in the fixture regime. With the real embedding that count is 4. On the tuned rows the same counts are 28 of 45 and 33 of 45. The head carries a command on 8 of the 24 sealed decline rows.\n\n#### The Limits of the Reading\n\n> The rates count a workflow opened before the first write, on tuned rows with one run each, so they do not show that the brief makes a model follow a correct workflow more often.\n\nA load is not a followed step. The Codex numbers are thin counts. No brief reached Codex in either arm.\n\n#### A Paired Arm Awaits Its Runs\n\nThe runner can run the same fresh rows with the advisor off and on. The scorer pairs the two arms on each row. A row only one arm scored counts as unpaired. The first run was stopped before any scoring, so it gives no rate yet.\n\n&nbsp;\n== vibe advisor module\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A Vibe session runs in a throwaway folder, so the checkout is located from\n// this file instead: vibe -> hooks -> system-skill-advisor -> skills -> .skilled -> root.\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n\nconst ADVISOR_MODULE_URL = new URL(\n  '../../runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js',\n  import.meta.url,\n).href;\n\n// Mirrors the advisor renderer's directive label. A brief that drifts past it is\n// never split, so it is always delivered whole.\nconst DIRECTIVE_SEPARATOR = '\\nDirectives:';\nconst CHILD_SESSION_ENV = 'AI_SESSION_CHILD';\n  write(sessionId, context);\n  return context;\n}\n\nasync function runAdvisor(input) {\n  const advisor = await import(ADVISOR_MODULE_URL);\n  return advisor.handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit(input, {\n    runtime: ADVISOR_RUNTIME,\n    writeDiagnostic: () => {},\n  });\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CORE LOGIC\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Build the advisor part of one turn-start context.\n *\n * @param {Object} payload - The Vibe pre_agent payload.\n * @param {Object} [dependencies] - Injectable for deterministic tests.\n== health writer name\n442:export function serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record: AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord): string {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Workflow Measure\n\n#### Six Paths and Two Rates\n\nThe transcript summary sorts each run into one path. `command` means it read the command's own document, or the host expanded it first. `skill` means it loaded the owning skill's `SKILL.md` or `ROUTER.md`. `otherMode` means it loaded another mode under the same hub. `asked` means the run offered the command and waited. `improvised` means it wrote without loading either. `none` means it loaded nothing and wrote nothing. `loadRate` counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run. `followedRate` adds `asked` to `command` and `skill` over every owned scored run. On the stored final arm the followed rate reads claude 8 of 16 and devin 16 of 16. It reads dsh 13 of 15, opencode 14 of 16 and pi 12 of 16.\n\n#### Every Shape a Load Takes\n\nA load is a read tool, a skill tool or a shell read. The shell readers include `cat`, `sed -n` and `head`. An in-place `sed` is not a read. A `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror counts too. On Codex, one `exec_command` body counts as one shell step.\n\n#### What Does Not Count\n\nA search is not a load, and neither is a heredoc line. A write outside the checkout, such as a temp note, no longer sets the boundary for a load.\n\n#### The Counts on Sealed Rows\n\nNobody tuned the 44 sealed plain rows. The brief carries the right command 1 time in the fixture regime. With the real embedding that count is 4. On the tuned rows the same counts are 28 of 45 and 33 of 45. The head carries a command on 8 of the 24 sealed decline rows.\n\n#### The Limits of the Reading\n\n> The rates count a workflow opened before the first write, on tuned rows with one run each, so they do not show that the brief makes a model follow a correct workflow more often.\n\nA load is not a followed step. The Codex numbers are thin counts. No brief reached Codex in either arm.\n\n#### A Paired Arm Awaits Its Runs\n\nThe runner can run the same fresh rows with the advisor off and on. The scorer pairs the two arms on each row. A row only one arm scored counts as unpaired. The first run was stopped before any scoring, so it gives no rate yet.\n\n&nbsp;\n== vibe advisor module\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A Vibe session runs in a throwaway folder, so the checkout is located from\n// this file instead: vibe -> hooks -> system-skill-advisor -> skills -> .skilled -> root.\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n\nconst ADVISOR_MODULE_URL = new URL(\n  '../../runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js',\n  import.meta.url,\n).href;\n\n// Mirrors the advisor renderer's directive label. A brief that drifts past it is\n// never split, so it is always delivered whole.\nconst DIRECTIVE_SEPARATOR = '\\nDirectives:';\nconst CHILD_SESSION_ENV = 'AI_SESSION_CHILD';\n  write(sessionId, context);\n  return context;\n}\n\nasync function runAdvisor(input) {\n  const advisor = await import(ADVISOR_MODULE_URL);\n  return advisor.handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit(input, {\n    runtime: ADVISOR_RUNTIME,\n    writeDiagnostic: () => {},\n  });\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CORE LOGIC\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Build the advisor part of one turn-start context.\n *\n * @param {Object} payload - The Vibe pre_agent payload.\n * @param {Object} [dependencies] - Injectable for deterministic tests.\n== health writer name\n442:export function serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record: AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord): string {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\nsed -n '172,200p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\\necho \\\"== vibe advisor module\\\"; sed -n '24,40p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs; sed -n '180,200p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs\\necho \\\"== health writer name\\\"; grep -n \\\"export.*record\\\\|appendAdvisorHookDiagnostic\\\\|writeAdvisorHook\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761603777,"end":1794761605148}}}}
