{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761610999,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"id":"prt_1e020d6f7001Y3ni8oXROwQj3l","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e020caa6001mPnEJDFRk7MaQu","type":"step-start","snapshot":"61ba4da581e50173edc85896300c6b2e592e6e1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761641853,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e020ff6a0020DcVPLXO84KHGb","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e020caa6001mPnEJDFRk7MaQu","type":"tool","id":"call_22d7baeb299648acb1030343","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dimension\n\nPrimary dimension: **correctness**. The pass checked whether the changelog's workflow-measure formulas and path vocabulary describe what `score-command-transcripts.mjs` actually computes, including the Vibe journal path the operator focus names.\n\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus asks whether the transcript scorer counts a load, a followed step or an offer that did not happen, including Vibe journal records. This iteration read the `Workflow Measure` section line by line against the scorer's `workflowPath()` union, its `loadRate` and `followedRate` expressions, and its Vibe journal loader. No prompt corpus was opened; the check is code-and-formula only.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `docs-metadata-5`.\n- Session: `fanout-docs-metadata-5-1794760565927-i99t40`, generation 1, new lineage.\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes. Consumed: 4 calls, about 2 minutes.\n- Prior state: 7 open P2 findings, 0 P0, 0 P1; traceability and maintainability covered.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:172-198`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:883-940` (`askedAndWaited`, `workflowPath`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1840-1895` (published `workflow` tally and rates)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1645-1650` (Vibe journal load)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:180-190` (Vibe diagnostic writer)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:32-44`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The load-rate sentence and the \"six paths\" heading do not match the published tally** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176` -- The note says `loadRate` \"counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run\" and heads the section \"Six Paths and Two Rates\". The scorer's `loadRate` numerator is `command + skill` only, so an `otherMode` run — a run that loaded another mode under the same hub, which the same note calls a load — is counted in the denominator but not the numerator. The published `workflow` tally also carries a seventh path, `noOwner`, which the note never mentions.\n   - Case: an arm of 10 owned runs scores `command=6`, `skill=2`, `otherMode=2`, with `asked`, `improvised` and `none` at 0. A reader applying the note's \"loaded a workflow\" definition expects `loadRate=1.0`; the scorer reports `8/10 = 0.8`, because the two `otherMode` runs loaded a different mode.\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1863]` (the `loadRate` numerator is `command + skill`); `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857]` (`noOwner` is published in the same `workflow` object); `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:914]` (`workflowPath` returns seven values).\n   - User impact: a release reader cannot recompute `loadRate` from the counts the note describes, and a run that opened a workflow under another mode is silently a non-load in the published rate.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: the formula appears once in the note; the scorer has one `loadRate` construction and one `workflowPath` union, so the mismatch is a single definition gap rather than a second convention.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"changelog: workflow measure\", \"transcript scorer loadRate\", \"transcript scorer workflow tally\"]\n   - Recommendation: say \"`loadRate` counts the runs that loaded the expected command or skill; an `otherMode` run loaded a different workflow and stays out of the numerator\", and list `noOwner` as the seventh path or state that it is excluded from the owned denominator.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | No top-level spec reference; phase child `019-workflow-outcome-measure` and `022-workflow-measure-soundness` own the measure's intent. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The note's runtime list matches the handlers that write health records; Vibe passes a no-op diagnostic writer. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The Vibe journal loader and the Vibe diagnostic writer were read at their exact call sites. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | No catalog claim changed this iteration. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file changed this iteration. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `workflowPath()` returns `command`, `skill`, `otherMode`, `asked`, `improvised`, `none` and `noOwner`; the note documents the first six.\n- `loadRate` is `rate(command + skill, command + skill + asked + otherMode + improvised + none)`; `followedRate` is `rate(command + skill + asked, ...same denominator)`.\n- The `asked` path requires `policy === ASK_POLICY`, `wrote !== true`, no write position and `askedAndWaited(stream, command)`, so an offer that did not happen is not counted as a followed step.\n- Vibe records go through `loadVibeSession()` and `vibeRecords()` before `workflowPath()`, so the Vibe journal is scored by the same path function rather than a parallel one.\n- Vibe's `runAdvisor` passes `writeDiagnostic: () => {}`, which is why the changelog's six-runtime list and its OpenCode exclusion are accurate without naming Vibe.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `otherMode` could be read as \"not a load\" because it is a different workflow. That reading is defensible for `followedRate`, but the note's own definition of the path says it \"loaded another mode\", and `loadRate` is described as runs that \"loaded a workflow\", so the sentence is broader than the numerator under either reading.\n- The seventh path `noOwner` may be considered internal because it is excluded from every rate denominator. It is still published in the summary object, so a reader reconciling counts will meet a bucket the note does not define.\n- The stored per-runtime rates (claude 8 of 16, and so on) were not re-derived; the stored arm data is outside this lineage's scope and was not opened. The finding is about the formula definition, not those numbers.\n- No prompt corpus was opened. Holdout hygiene holds.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `followedRate` matches the note exactly: `asked` is added to `command` and `skill`, over the six-path owned denominator.\n- `asked` is not counted when no offer happened: the branch requires an ask policy, no write and an observed ask-and-wait event.\n- A search and a heredoc line are not loads; the normalizer's comment and the note agree.\n- The Vibe journal is loaded through `loadVibeSession()` and normalized with `vibeRecords()`; no parallel Vibe-only path classifier exists.\n- The health-record runtime list is accurate: Vibe calls the Claude handler with a no-op `writeDiagnostic`, so it writes no record and is correctly absent from the list.\n- No scope violation occurred; no file outside the lineage directory was written.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- An offer counted as a followed step without an offer: ruled out; the `asked` branch requires `askedAndWaited`.\n- A non-load counted in `loadRate`: ruled out; the numerator is `command + skill`, both witnessed loads.\n- A separate Vibe scoring path: ruled out; Vibe records feed the same `workflowPath()`.\n- A missing runtime in the health-record list: ruled out; the two runtimes that do not write (Vibe, OpenCode) are either no-op or explicitly excluded.\n- A `followedRate` formula mismatch: ruled out; the numerator and denominator match the note.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene and prompt-leak claims across the scoped documents, plus the direct-call kill-switch sentence in `advisor-recommend.md` against the CLI's call order and the launcher's environment handling.\n- Reason: the operator focus names holdout hygiene and the direct-call switch, and those are the only security-flavored claims not yet checked.\n- Rotation status: traceability, maintainability and correctness completed; security remains.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — formula-to-code comparison found a real definition gap.\n- Required evidence: the scoped documents' holdout references, the CLI's `advisorDisabledBy` call order, and the launcher's environment allowlist.\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nPrimary dimension: **correctness**. The pass checked whether the changelog's workflow-measure formulas and path vocabulary describe what `score-command-transcripts.mjs` actually computes, including the Vibe journal path the operator focus names.\\n\\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus asks whether the transcript scorer counts a load, a followed step or an offer that did not happen, including Vibe journal records. This iteration read the `Workflow Measure` section line by line against the scorer's `workflowPath()` union, its `loadRate` and `followedRate` expressions, and its Vibe journal loader. No prompt corpus was opened; the check is code-and-formula only.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `docs-metadata-5`.\\n- Session: `fanout-docs-metadata-5-1794760565927-i99t40`, generation 1, new lineage.\\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes. Consumed: 4 calls, about 2 minutes.\\n- Prior state: 7 open P2 findings, 0 P0, 0 P1; traceability and maintainability covered.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:172-198`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:883-940` (`askedAndWaited`, `workflowPath`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1840-1895` (published `workflow` tally and rates)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1645-1650` (Vibe journal load)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:180-190` (Vibe diagnostic writer)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:32-44`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The load-rate sentence and the \\\"six paths\\\" heading do not match the published tally** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176` -- The note says `loadRate` \\\"counts the runs that loaded a workflow over every owned run\\\" and heads the section \\\"Six Paths and Two Rates\\\". The scorer's `loadRate` numerator is `command + skill` only, so an `otherMode` run — a run that loaded another mode under the same hub, which the same note calls a load — is counted in the denominator but not the numerator. The published `workflow` tally also carries a seventh path, `noOwner`, which the note never mentions.\\n   - Case: an arm of 10 owned runs scores `command=6`, `skill=2`, `otherMode=2`, with `asked`, `improvised` and `none` at 0. A reader applying the note's \\\"loaded a workflow\\\" definition expects `loadRate=1.0`; the scorer reports `8/10 = 0.8`, because the two `otherMode` runs loaded a different mode.\\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:176]`; `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1863]` (the `loadRate` numerator is `command + skill`); `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857]` (`noOwner` is published in the same `workflow` object); `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:914]` (`workflowPath` returns seven values).\\n   - User impact: a release reader cannot recompute `loadRate` from the counts the note describes, and a run that opened a workflow under another mode is silently a non-load in the published rate.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: the formula appears once in the note; the scorer has one `loadRate` construction and one `workflowPath` union, so the mismatch is a single definition gap rather than a second convention.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"changelog: workflow measure\\\", \\\"transcript scorer loadRate\\\", \\\"transcript scorer workflow tally\\\"]\\n   - Recommendation: say \\\"`loadRate` counts the runs that loaded the expected command or skill; an `otherMode` run loaded a different workflow and stays out of the numerator\\\", and list `noOwner` as the seventh path or state that it is excluded from the owned denominator.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | No top-level spec reference; phase child `019-workflow-outcome-measure` and `022-workflow-measure-soundness` own the measure's intent. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No top-level `checklist.md`. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The note's runtime list matches the handlers that write health records; Vibe passes a no-op diagnostic writer. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The Vibe journal loader and the Vibe diagnostic writer were read at their exact call sites. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | No catalog claim changed this iteration. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook file changed this iteration. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `workflowPath()` returns `command`, `skill`, `otherMode`, `asked`, `improvised`, `none` and `noOwner`; the note documents the first six.\\n- `loadRate` is `rate(command + skill, command + skill + asked + otherMode + improvised + none)`; `followedRate` is `rate(command + skill + asked, ...same denominator)`.\\n- The `asked` path requires `policy === ASK_POLICY`, `wrote !== true`, no write position and `askedAndWaited(stream, command)`, so an offer that did not happen is not counted as a followed step.\\n- Vibe records go through `loadVibeSession()` and `vibeRecords()` before `workflowPath()`, so the Vibe journal is scored by the same path function rather than a parallel one.\\n- Vibe's `runAdvisor` passes `writeDiagnostic: () => {}`, which is why the changelog's six-runtime list and its OpenCode exclusion are accurate without naming Vibe.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `otherMode` could be read as \\\"not a load\\\" because it is a different workflow. That reading is defensible for `followedRate`, but the note's own definition of the path says it \\\"loaded another mode\\\", and `loadRate` is described as runs that \\\"loaded a workflow\\\", so the sentence is broader than the numerator under either reading.\\n- The seventh path `noOwner` may be considered internal because it is excluded from every rate denominator. It is still published in the summary object, so a reader reconciling counts will meet a bucket the note does not define.\\n- The stored per-runtime rates (claude 8 of 16, and so on) were not re-derived; the stored arm data is outside this lineage's scope and was not opened. The finding is about the formula definition, not those numbers.\\n- No prompt corpus was opened. Holdout hygiene holds.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `followedRate` matches the note exactly: `asked` is added to `command` and `skill`, over the six-path owned denominator.\\n- `asked` is not counted when no offer happened: the branch requires an ask policy, no write and an observed ask-and-wait event.\\n- A search and a heredoc line are not loads; the normalizer's comment and the note agree.\\n- The Vibe journal is loaded through `loadVibeSession()` and normalized with `vibeRecords()`; no parallel Vibe-only path classifier exists.\\n- The health-record runtime list is accurate: Vibe calls the Claude handler with a no-op `writeDiagnostic`, so it writes no record and is correctly absent from the list.\\n- No scope violation occurred; no file outside the lineage directory was written.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- An offer counted as a followed step without an offer: ruled out; the `asked` branch requires `askedAndWaited`.\\n- A non-load counted in `loadRate`: ruled out; the numerator is `command + skill`, both witnessed loads.\\n- A separate Vibe scoring path: ruled out; Vibe records feed the same `workflowPath()`.\\n- A missing runtime in the health-record list: ruled out; the two runtimes that do not write (Vibe, OpenCode) are either no-op or explicitly excluded.\\n- A `followedRate` formula mismatch: ruled out; the numerator and denominator match the note.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene and prompt-leak claims across the scoped documents, plus the direct-call kill-switch sentence in `advisor-recommend.md` against the CLI's call order and the launcher's environment handling.\\n- Reason: the operator focus names holdout hygiene and the direct-call switch, and those are the only security-flavored claims not yet checked.\\n- Rotation status: traceability, maintainability and correctness completed; security remains.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — formula-to-code comparison found a real definition gap.\\n- Required evidence: the scoped documents' holdout references, the CLI's `advisorDisabledBy` call order, and the launcher's environment allowlist.\\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-metadata-5/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761621354,"end":1794761641853}}}}
