{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761701254,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0222dba00139W6j6e35WjEVK","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd3ffeb90jQTuAVj0Ap9","messageID":"msg_1e02209b1001unbGjhzNdDN9w8","type":"tool","id":"call_d6c3e3b3f8224a2889938832","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\necho \"== CLI disable order\"; grep -n \"advisorDisabledBy\\|daemon\\|connect\\|local scorer\\|runLocal\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts | head -25\necho \"== launcher env\"; grep -n \"DISABLED\\|env\\|delete\\|omit\" .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs | head -25\necho \"== holdout refs in scope docs\"; grep -rn \"holdout-prompts\\|command-prompts\\|behaviour-fresh-prompts\\|split.*holdout\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/*/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md 2>/dev/null | head"},"output":"== CLI disable order\n33:// A cold call starts the daemon and waits for it, but never past this. The measured\n35:// tool timeout on a daemon that never accepted a connection — not from waiting at all.\n37:// The launcher's lease, which records when the running daemon was launched.\n42:// The CLI's own last resort when no daemon answers: the checked-in Python scorer\n43:// still routes locally, so an unreachable daemon degrades a recommendation\n806:  return `skill-advisor - daemon-backed CLI for system-skill-advisor\n832:  0 success, 1 runtime error, 64 usage/schema error, 69 protocol mismatch, 75 retryable daemon error`;\n1142:      launcherState.reason = `daemon launcher failed to start: ${error.message}`;\n1147:        ? `daemon launcher exited on ${signal}`\n1148:        : `daemon launcher exited with code ${code ?? 'unknown'}`;\n1154:    // Probe before reading the launcher state: a launcher that bridged to a daemon which\n1180:  static connect(socketPath: string, bridge: BridgeModule, timeoutMs: number): Promise<JsonRpcSocketClient> {\n1188:        socket.off?.('connect', onConnect);\n1199:      const timer = setTimeout(() => finish(new CliRetryableError('connection timed out')), timeoutMs);\n1203:        const connectionOptions = bridge.toConnectionOptions(socketPath);\n1204:        socket = typeof connectionOptions === 'string'\n1205:          ? net.createConnection(connectionOptions)\n1206:          : net.createConnection(connectionOptions);\n1212:      socket.once('connect', onConnect);\n1291:// A daemon loads its code once at launch, so after a rebuild a live daemon still answers\n1292:// with the old code. Only a launched daemon counts: the lease carries a childPid once\n1310:// A launcher started next to a stale daemon recycles it. The call waits for the lease to\n1311:// show the replacement rather than connecting to the daemon being retired. A launcher\n1312:// that exits with the old daemon still in place skipped the recycle, so the call uses\n1313:// that daemon as it always did.\n== launcher env\n1:#!/usr/bin/env node\n39:// Load project-local env overrides BEFORE spawning the daemon child. .env.local wins over\n40:// .env, both are gitignored. Existing process.env wins over file values (do not override).\n57:    if (!(key in process.env)) {\n58:      process.env[key] = val;\n70:for (const fname of ['.env.local', '.env']) {\n74:    if (n > 0) process.stderr.write(`[system-skill-advisor-launcher] loaded ${n} env(s) from ${fname}\\n`);\n78:// Repo policy defaults, applied only when the environment stays silent. These\n81:// and the repository opts into its own values here. A live environment value or\n82:// a .env entry still wins, so an operator can override or disable either one.\n88:  if (!(key in process.env)) {\n89:    process.env[key] = value;\n147:  // Compiled-routing runtime flag. Without this literal key the operator's .env\n168:  // the scorer's env reader never sees them under normal daemon supervision\n180:  'SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED',\n213:        if (process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR?.startsWith('tcp://')) {\n214:          return process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR;\n216:        const socketDir = process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\n217:          ? path.resolve(process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR)\n222:        const socketDir = process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\n223:          ? path.resolve(process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR)\n228:        if (process.env.SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED === '1' && legacyReport) {\n303:  if (process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG === '1') {\n312:function createChildEnv(sourceEnv = process.env) {\n338:      { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir(), env: sourceEnv },\n== holdout refs in scope docs\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"== CLI disable order\n33:// A cold call starts the daemon and waits for it, but never past this. The measured\n35:// tool timeout on a daemon that never accepted a connection — not from waiting at all.\n37:// The launcher's lease, which records when the running daemon was launched.\n42:// The CLI's own last resort when no daemon answers: the checked-in Python scorer\n43:// still routes locally, so an unreachable daemon degrades a recommendation\n806:  return `skill-advisor - daemon-backed CLI for system-skill-advisor\n832:  0 success, 1 runtime error, 64 usage/schema error, 69 protocol mismatch, 75 retryable daemon error`;\n1142:      launcherState.reason = `daemon launcher failed to start: ${error.message}`;\n1147:        ? `daemon launcher exited on ${signal}`\n1148:        : `daemon launcher exited with code ${code ?? 'unknown'}`;\n1154:    // Probe before reading the launcher state: a launcher that bridged to a daemon which\n1180:  static connect(socketPath: string, bridge: BridgeModule, timeoutMs: number): Promise<JsonRpcSocketClient> {\n1188:        socket.off?.('connect', onConnect);\n1199:      const timer = setTimeout(() => finish(new CliRetryableError('connection timed out')), timeoutMs);\n1203:        const connectionOptions = bridge.toConnectionOptions(socketPath);\n1204:        socket = typeof connectionOptions === 'string'\n1205:          ? net.createConnection(connectionOptions)\n1206:          : net.createConnection(connectionOptions);\n1212:      socket.once('connect', onConnect);\n1291:// A daemon loads its code once at launch, so after a rebuild a live daemon still answers\n1292:// with the old code. Only a launched daemon counts: the lease carries a childPid once\n1310:// A launcher started next to a stale daemon recycles it. The call waits for the lease to\n1311:// show the replacement rather than connecting to the daemon being retired. A launcher\n1312:// that exits with the old daemon still in place skipped the recycle, so the call uses\n1313:// that daemon as it always did.\n== launcher env\n1:#!/usr/bin/env node\n39:// Load project-local env overrides BEFORE spawning the daemon child. .env.local wins over\n40:// .env, both are gitignored. Existing process.env wins over file values (do not override).\n57:    if (!(key in process.env)) {\n58:      process.env[key] = val;\n70:for (const fname of ['.env.local', '.env']) {\n74:    if (n > 0) process.stderr.write(`[system-skill-advisor-launcher] loaded ${n} env(s) from ${fname}\\n`);\n78:// Repo policy defaults, applied only when the environment stays silent. These\n81:// and the repository opts into its own values here. A live environment value or\n82:// a .env entry still wins, so an operator can override or disable either one.\n88:  if (!(key in process.env)) {\n89:    process.env[key] = value;\n147:  // Compiled-routing runtime flag. Without this literal key the operator's .env\n168:  // the scorer's env reader never sees them under normal daemon supervision\n180:  'SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED',\n213:        if (process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR?.startsWith('tcp://')) {\n214:          return process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR;\n216:        const socketDir = process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\n217:          ? path.resolve(process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR)\n222:        const socketDir = process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\n223:          ? path.resolve(process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR)\n228:        if (process.env.SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED === '1' && legacyReport) {\n303:  if (process.env.SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG === '1') {\n312:function createChildEnv(sourceEnv = process.env) {\n338:      { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir(), env: sourceEnv },\n== holdout refs in scope docs\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\necho \\\"== CLI disable order\\\"; grep -n \\\"advisorDisabledBy\\\\|daemon\\\\|connect\\\\|local scorer\\\\|runLocal\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts | head -25\\necho \\\"== launcher env\\\"; grep -n \\\"DISABLED\\\\|env\\\\|delete\\\\|omit\\\" .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs | head -25\\necho \\\"== holdout refs in scope docs\\\"; grep -rn \\\"holdout-prompts\\\\|command-prompts\\\\|behaviour-fresh-prompts\\\\|split.*holdout\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/*/*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md 2>/dev/null | head\"}"},"time":{"s