\"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2189:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2190:   consecutive_failures: \"See step_check_convergence rule 1a. The script counts trailing failed iterations from the state log and returns stop reason error.\"\n2191:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2192: \n2193: # ────────\n2194: # RULES\n2195: # ────────\n2196: rules:\n2197:   DRY_RUN_OVERRIDES:\n2198:     - \"When dry_run is true, dry_run_control overrides default dispatch, write, reducer, continuity-save, and child-spawn requirements.\"\n2199:     - \"Dry-run preview events are emitted to terminal output only and are not persisted.\"\n2200:   ALWAYS:\n2201:     - follow_workflow_phases_in_order\n2202:     - dispatch_deep_review_agent_per_iteration\n2203:     - check_convergence_before_each_iteration\n2204:     - write_all_state_to_files\n2205:     - write_continuity_after_synthesis\n2206:     - respect_max_iterations_cap\n2207:     - treat_review_target_as_read_only\n2208:     - deduplicate_findings_before_synthesis\n2209:     - run_adversarial_selfcheck_on_p0_p1\n2210:   NEVER:\n2211:     - skip_convergence_check\n2212:     - dispatch_non_leaf_agents\n2213:     - hold_iteration_findings_in_memory_only\n2214:     - modify_config_after_initialization\n2215:     - overwrite_jsonl_state_log\n2216:     - proceed_without_state_file_verification\n2217:     - modify_files_under_review\n2218:     - report_p0_without_file_line_evidence\n2219: \n2220: # ────────\n2221: # REFERENCE-ONLY APPENDIX\n2222: # ────────\n2223: reference_only_appendix:\n2224:   checkpoint_commit:\n2225:     note: \"Checkpoint commits are intentionally excluded from workflow.steps.\"\n2226:     commands:\n2227:       - \"git add {state_paths.iteration_pattern} {state_paths.state_log} {state_paths.findings_registry} {state_paths.strategy} {state_paths.review_output}\"\n2228:       - 'git commit -m \"chore(deep-review): iteration {NNN} complete\" -m \"{one-line summary of what the iteration found}\"'\n2229:   severity_weights:\n2230:     note: \"Severity weights for newFindingsRatio calculation\"\n2231:     weights:\n2232:       P0: 10.0\n2233:       P1: 5.0\n2234:       P2: 1.0\n2235:     p0_override: \"If ANY new P0 discovered → newFindingsRatio = max(calculated, 0.50). A single new P0 blocks convergence.\"\n2236:     clean_pass: \"If total_findings == 0 (clean pass) → newFindingsRatio = 0.0\"\n2237:   review_dimensions:\n2238:     note: \"All 4 default review dimensions with priority ordering\"\n2239:     dimensions:\n2240:       - { priority: 1, name: \"correctness\", checks: \"Logic, state flow, edge cases, error handling\" }\n2241:       - { priority: 2, name: \"security\", checks: \"Auth, input/output safety, data exposure, permissions\" }\n2242:       - { priority: 3, name: \"traceability\", checks: \"Spec/checklist alignment, cross-reference integrity, evidence coverage\" }\n2243:       - { priority: 4, name: \"maintainability\", checks: \"Patterns, documentation quality, safe follow-on change clarity\" }\n2244:   cross_reference_protocols:\n2245:     note: \"Cross-reference verification protocols split into core and overlay classes\"\n2246:     core_protocols:\n2247:       - { check: \"Spec vs Code\", source: \"spec.md claims\", target: \"implementation\" }\n2248:       - { check: \"Checklist vs Evidence\", source: \"[x] items\", target: \"cited evidence\" }\n2249:     overlay_protocols:\n2250:       - { check: \"SKILL.md vs Agent\", source: \"Skill contracts\", target: \"agent files\" }\n2251:       - { check: \"Agent Cross-Runtime\", source: \".claude\", target: \".opencode/.agents\" }\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2252]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limi